Open an SSH session to the container of a running training job, optionally targeting a specific node by index.

Prerequisite: the job must have been submitted with an SSH service enabled in its YAML, e.g.:

  services:
    my_ssh:
      type: ssh
      ssh_public_keys: |
        ssh-ed25519 AAAA... user@host

The SSH service must reach 'Running' status before this command can connect; that typically takes 30s–120s after the job enters Running. If --private-key-file-path is omitted, the OpenSSH client falls back to the default identities under ~/.ssh/.

Usage
  azd ai training job connect-ssh [flags]

Flags
      --name string                  : Job name (required)
      --node-index int               : Zero-based index of the node to connect to in a multi-node job (default 0)
      --private-key-file-path string : Path to the SSH private key file (optional; ssh will use ~/.ssh defaults if omitted)

Global Flags
  -C, --cwd string              : Sets the current working directory
      --debug                   : Enables debug and diagnostics logging
  -e, --environment string      : The name of the environment to use
  -h, --help                    : help for connect-ssh
      --no-prompt               : Runs without prompts. Uses existing values; fails if any required value or decision cannot be resolved automatically.
  -o, --output string           : The output format (default "default")
      --project-endpoint string : Azure AI Foundry project endpoint URL (e.g., https://account.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/project-name)
  -s, --subscription string     : Azure subscription ID (enables implicit init if environment not configured)

Examples
  Connect to the first node with a specific SSH key
    azd ai training job connect-ssh --name my-job --node-index 0 --private-key-file-path ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
